SUMMARY:Earth Day Celebration
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a day dedicated to local agriculture\, sustainability\, biodiversity\, and community that can lead to a better tomorrow for our planet.\n\n\n\nWe are thrilled to partner with and host SoundsTruck NW at the market for this special event. Their mobile stage will transform into a concert stage\, kitchen\, and learning lab: \n\n\n\n\n\n9 AM — Coffee Talk: Brewing a Better World with Slow Food Coffee Coalition and SUNAO Coffee & Cacao\n\n\n\n10 AM — Farmer’s Talk: Planting Seeds of Resilience with Nick Canino\, Rhythm Seed Farm \n\n\n\n11 AM — Storytime with Live Music: Stories of Earth and Time with Leslie Barnard Booth\n\n\n\n12 PM — Chef’s Talk & Cooking Live Demo: Food as Medicine with Chef Naoko\n\n\n\n1 PM — Live Music: Echoes of Nature – Sounds of Japan with Maido Mind\n\n\n\n\n\nEngage with participating vendors and visiting community partners and anytime between 9 AM to 2 PM: \n\n\n\n\nFood Waves: Learn about food justice and how to grow your own microgreens with Farmer Matt Brown.\n\n\n\nUrban Gleaners: Learn how they reimagine food waste and fight hunger.\n\n\n\nPSU Smallwood Food Pantry: Explore ways you can support community food security. \n\n\n\nThe Xerces Society for Invertebrate Conservation: Don’t miss the chance to make unique pollinator crafts\, engage in fun educational games\, and discover valuable resources for creating your own pollinator-friendly garden.\n\n\n\n\nAnd from 11 am to 1 pm\, our goat milk vendor\, Cottage Hill Farm will have their baby goats!
URL:https://www.portlandfarmersmarket.org/event/earth-day-celebration/
LOCATION:PSU Farmers Market\, SW Park & Montgomery\, Portland\, OR\, 97201\, United States
CATEGORIES:PSU Farmers Market
